# Tests for the Ctc_odc module

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete case, worked by hand
from IRC 24, Schedule 8812 (`f1040s8--2024.pdf`) and its instructions
(`i1040s8--2024.pdf`) as quoted in `catala/ctc_odc.catala_en`. Every scope
sets satisfiable inputs and asserts the expected result; most also assert
that a known-bad output (the value a plausible mistake would give) is not
produced. The oracle comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=ctc_odc`,
`make difftest SCOPE=ctc_odc_household` and `make difftest-persons`.

> Using Types
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R
> Using Eitc as E
> Using Ctc_odc as C

## Helper: one household member

The default is the filer's biological son, born 2014-05-10 (10 at the end of
2024), a U.S. citizen with an SSN whose card has no restriction, who lived
with the filer all year, did not provide over half of his own support, is
unmarried, nobody else's qualifying child, and claimed. The filer was born
1985-06-15, is a U.S. citizen and cannot be claimed by anyone. A test
overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope MkChild:
  context relationship content Q.Relationship
  context date_of_birth content date
  context residency_duration content Q.ResidencyDuration
  context tin_type content R.TinType
  context citizen content boolean
  context us_resident content boolean
  context canada_mexico_resident content boolean
  context ssn_employment_validity content C.SsnEmploymentValidity
  context tp_claims content boolean
  context gross_income content money
  context qr_support content boolean
  output household_member content C.HouseholdMember
  output result content C.CtcOdcPersonTest

scope MkChild:
  definition relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition date_of_birth equals |2014-05-10|
  definition residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition tin_type equals R.TinType.Ssn
  definition citizen equals true
  definition us_resident equals false
  definition canada_mexico_resident equals false
  definition ssn_employment_validity equals C.SsnEmploymentValidity.Neither
  definition tp_claims equals true
  definition gross_income equals $0
  definition qr_support equals true
  definition household_member equals C.HouseholdMember {
    -- member: R.Member {
      -- person: Q.Person {
           -- relationship: relationship
           -- date_of_birth: date_of_birth
           -- full_time_student: false
           -- permanent_total_disability: false
           -- residency_duration: residency_duration
           -- own_support: false
           -- married: false
           -- writable_joint_return: false
           -- writable_required_to_file: false
           -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
           -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
      -- answers: R.DependentAnswers {
           -- gross_income: gross_income
           -- writable_qr_support_test: qr_support
           -- tin_type: tin_type
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: citizen
           -- writable_us_resident: us_resident
           -- writable_us_national: false
           -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: canada_mexico_resident
           -- tp_claims: tp_claims
           -- tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc: false
           -- disqualified_due_to_parental_custody: false } }
    -- ssn_employment_validity: ssn_employment_validity }
  definition result equals
    output of C.CtcOdcPersonTest with {
      -- household_member: household_member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
```

## Per-person tests (IRC 24(c), (h)(4), (h)(7))

### A 10-year-old son with a valid SSN: CTC, not ODC

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonCtcChild:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonCtcChild:
  assertion c.result.dependent.qualifying_child
  assertion c.result.ssn_valid_for_employment
  assertion c.result.eligible_ctc
  # Known-bad: the same person is never counted for both credits
  assertion not c.result.eligible_odc
```

### Born 2007-12-31: 17 at the end of 2024, ODC, not CTC

IRC 24(c)(1) "who has not attained age 17"; instructions p 2, Example 1
(turned 17 on December 30, 2024: no CTC). The son is still a qualifying child
(under 19), so he is a dependent for the ODC.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonAge17:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonAge17:
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |2007-12-31|
  assertion c.result.dependent.qc.age = 17
  assertion c.result.dependent.qualifying_child
  assertion not c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion c.result.eligible_odc
```

### Born 2008-01-01: 16 at the end of 2024, CTC

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonAge16:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonAge16:
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |2008-01-01|
  assertion c.result.dependent.qc.age = 16
  assertion c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion not c.result.eligible_odc
```

### A qualifying child with an ITIN: ODC (IRC 24(h)(7), (h)(4)(C))

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonItin:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonItin:
  definition c.tin_type equals R.TinType.Itin
  assertion c.result.dependent.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion not c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion c.result.eligible_odc
```

### SSN card "Not valid for employment": ODC

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonSsnNotValid:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonSsnNotValid:
  definition c.ssn_employment_validity equals C.SsnEmploymentValidity.NotValid
  assertion not c.result.ssn_valid_for_employment
  assertion not c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion c.result.eligible_odc
```

### SSN card "Valid for work only with DHS authorization"

The required SSN only while the authorization is in effect (instructions
p 1, "valid for employment").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonDhsAuthorization:
  in_effect scope MkChild
  expired scope MkChild

scope TestPersonDhsAuthorization:
  definition in_effect.ssn_employment_validity equals
    C.SsnEmploymentValidity.ValidOnlyWithDhsAuthorizationInEffect
  definition expired.ssn_employment_validity equals
    C.SsnEmploymentValidity.ValidOnlyWithDhsAuthorizationExpired
  assertion in_effect.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion not expired.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion expired.result.eligible_odc
```

### A nephew living in Mexico: a dependent, but neither CTC nor ODC

Instructions p 2, Example 2: "Your sibling's 10-year-old child lives in
Mexico and qualifies as your dependent. The child is not a U.S. citizen, U.S.
national, or U.S. resident alien. You can't use the child to claim the ODC."
IRC 24(c)(2), 24(h)(4)(B). The nephew lived with the filer for less than six
months, so he is the filer's qualifying relative (152(d)(2)(E)), not
qualifying child.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonMexicanNephew:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonMexicanNephew:
  definition c.relationship equals Q.Relationship.ChildOfSibling
  definition c.residency_duration equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition c.citizen equals false
  definition c.canada_mexico_resident equals true
  definition c.tin_type equals R.TinType.Itin
  assertion c.result.dependent.qualifying_relative
  assertion c.result.dependent.citizen_or_resident_test
  assertion c.result.dependent.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion not c.result.dependent.citizen_or_us_resident_test
  assertion not c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion not c.result.eligible_odc
```

### A child the filer does not claim: neither credit (IRC 24(a), "allowed a deduction under section 151")

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPersonNotClaimed:
  c scope MkChild

scope TestPersonNotClaimed:
  definition c.tp_claims equals false
  assertion c.result.dependent.qualifying_child
  assertion not c.result.eligible_ctc
  assertion not c.result.eligible_odc
```

### A household: counts for lines 4 and 6

Two CTC children, one 18-year-old student-age son (ODC) and one child with an
ITIN (ODC).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHouseholdCounts:
  a scope MkChild
  b scope MkChild
  older scope MkChild
  itin scope MkChild
  internal h content C.CtcOdcDependents

scope TestHouseholdCounts:
  definition b.date_of_birth equals |2020-02-29|
  definition older.date_of_birth equals |2006-03-01|
  definition itin.tin_type equals R.TinType.Itin
  definition h equals
    output of C.CtcOdcDependents with {
      -- household_members:
           [a.household_member; b.household_member; older.household_member;
            itin.household_member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion h.ctc_eligible_dependents = 2
  assertion h.odc_eligible_dependents = 2
```

### A filer who can be claimed as a dependent: no dependents, no credit

IRC 152(b)(1): such a filer is treated as having no dependents.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHouseholdFilerIsDependent:
  a scope MkChild
  internal h content C.CtcOdcDependents

scope TestHouseholdFilerIsDependent:
  definition h equals
    output of C.CtcOdcDependents with {
      -- household_members: [a.household_member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: true
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  assertion h.ctc_eligible_dependents = 0
  assertion h.odc_eligible_dependents = 0
```

## Helper: Schedule 8812 with default figures

Single, two CTC children, no ODC dependents, AGI and line 1z $100,000, line 18
tax $13,841 (the 2024 rate-schedule tax on $85,400 of taxable income,
single; the exact figure does not matter here), no other
credits, W-2 boxes 4 and 6 $7,650, no EIC, no combat pay, no improper
claims.

```catala
declaration scope Mk8812:
  context ctc content integer
  context odc content integer
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context agi content money
  context tax content money
  context cdcc content money
  context savers content money
  context edc content money
  context earned content money
  context combat_pay content money
  context ss_taxes content money
  context eic content money
  context received_improper_claims content boolean
  context notice content E.ImproperClaimsNotice
  context notice_expired content boolean
  output s content C.Schedule8812

scope Mk8812:
  definition ctc equals 2
  definition odc equals 0
  definition filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition agi equals $100,000
  definition tax equals $13,841
  definition cdcc equals $0
  definition savers equals $0
  definition edc equals $0
  definition earned equals $100,000
  definition combat_pay equals $0
  definition ss_taxes equals $7,650
  definition eic equals $0
  definition received_improper_claims equals false
  definition notice equals E.ImproperClaimsNotice.NotAnswered
  definition notice_expired equals false
  definition s equals
    output of C.Schedule8812 with {
      -- ctc_eligible_dependents: ctc
      -- odc_eligible_dependents: odc
      -- filing_status: filing_status
      -- agi: agi
      -- total_tentative_tax: tax
      -- cdcc_total_credit: cdcc
      -- qualified_saver_credit_amount: savers
      -- total_edc: edc
      -- employer_income_subtotal: earned
      -- all_combat_pay: combat_pay
      -- social_security_taxes_withheld: ss_taxes
      -- earned_income_credit: eic
      -- received_improper_claims: received_improper_claims
      -- received_improper_claims_notice: notice
      -- improper_claims_notice_expired: notice_expired
      -- has_filed_ctc_odc_since_notice_expired: false }
```

## Part I

### Two CTC children, single, AGI $100,000: $4,000

Lines 4-5: 2 x $2,000 = $4,000. Line 10: $0. Line 13: $13,841. Line 14:
$4,000. Line 16a: $0, so no ACTC.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812TwoKidsSingle100k:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812TwoKidsSingle100k:
  assertion m.s.total_potential_ctc = $4,000
  assertion m.s.total_potential_dependent_credits = $4,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $0
  assertion m.s.sched8812_credit_limit = $13,841
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $4,000
  assertion m.s.total_ctc = $4,000
  assertion m.s.total_odc = $0
  assertion m.s.remaining_ctc_and_odc = $0
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $0
  # Known-bad: the refundable cap is not paid on top of the full credit
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc != $3,400
```

### The same, limited by tax: line 14 is the tax, the rest is ACTC

Line 18 tax $3,000. Line 14 = $3,000. Line 16a = $1,000, line 16b = $3,400,
line 17 = $1,000. Line 19 = $97,500, line 20 = $14,625. Line 27 = $1,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812LimitedByTax:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812LimitedByTax:
  definition m.tax equals $3,000
  assertion m.s.sched8812_credit_limit = $3,000
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $3,000
  assertion m.s.remaining_ctc_and_odc = $1,000
  assertion m.s.total_potential_actc = $3,400
  assertion m.s.remaining_potential_actc = $1,000
  assertion m.s.regular_maximum_actc = $14,625
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $1,000
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc + m.s.additional_ctc = $4,000
```

### The credit limit subtracts the other nonrefundable credits

Credit Limit Worksheet A: line 1 $5,000 less Schedule 3 lines 2 ($600), 4
($400) and 6d ($1,000) is $3,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812CreditLimitOtherCredits:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812CreditLimitOtherCredits:
  definition m.tax equals $5,000
  definition m.cdcc equals $600
  definition m.savers equals $400
  definition m.edc equals $1,000
  assertion m.s.sched8812_credit_limit = $3,000
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $3,000
  # Known-bad: ignoring the other credits would give $4,000
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc != $4,000
```

### Phase-out, single, AGI $200,001: the $1 excess counts as $1,000

Line 10: $1 rounded up to $1,000; line 11: $50; line 12: $3,950.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812PhaseoutSingle200001:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812PhaseoutSingle200001:
  definition m.agi equals $200,001
  definition m.tax equals $40,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold = $200,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $1
  assertion m.s.rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $1,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $50
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_less_phaseout = $3,950
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $3,950
  # Known-bad: 5% of the unrounded excess ($0.05) is not the reduction
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout != $0
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc != $4,000
```

### Phase-out steps: $1,000 exactly stays $1,000, $1,001 is $2,000

Line 10 example: "if the result is $425, enter $1,000; if the result is
$1,025, enter $2,000".

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812PhaseoutSteps:
  at_200000 scope Mk8812
  at_200425 scope Mk8812
  at_201000 scope Mk8812
  at_201025 scope Mk8812

scope Test8812PhaseoutSteps:
  definition at_200000.agi equals $200,000
  definition at_200425.agi equals $200,425
  definition at_201000.agi equals $201,000
  definition at_201025.agi equals $201,025
  assertion at_200000.s.rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $0
  assertion at_200000.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $0
  assertion at_200425.s.rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $1,000
  assertion at_201000.s.rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $1,000
  assertion at_201000.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $50
  assertion at_201025.s.rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold = $2,000
  assertion at_201025.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $100
```

### MFJ threshold $400,000

MFJ at $400,000: no reduction; at $400,001: $50. Single at $400,000: excess
$200,000, reduction $10,000, more than the $4,000 credit: line 12 is $0, so
no CTC and no ACTC even with no tax.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812PhaseoutMfj:
  mfj_400000 scope Mk8812
  mfj_400001 scope Mk8812
  single_400000 scope Mk8812

scope Test8812PhaseoutMfj:
  definition mfj_400000.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_400000.agi equals $400,000
  definition mfj_400001.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_400001.agi equals $400,001
  definition single_400000.agi equals $400,000
  definition single_400000.tax equals $0
  assertion mfj_400000.s.dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold = $400,000
  assertion mfj_400000.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $0
  assertion mfj_400000.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $4,000
  assertion mfj_400001.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $50
  assertion mfj_400001.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $3,950
  assertion single_400000.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $10,000
  assertion single_400000.s.dependent_credit_less_phaseout = $0
  assertion not single_400000.s.dependent_credit_not_fully_phased_out
  assertion single_400000.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $0
  assertion single_400000.s.additional_ctc = $0
```

### Qualifying surviving spouse uses $200,000 (no joint return)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812PhaseoutQss:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812PhaseoutQss:
  definition m.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  definition m.agi equals $250,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold = $200,000
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $2,500
```

### The phase-out reduces the ODC first

One CTC child and one ODC dependent: line 8 = $2,500. AGI $210,000 single:
line 11 = $500, line 12 = $2,000. The ODC part is $0 and the CTC part
$2,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812OdcReducedFirst:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812OdcReducedFirst:
  definition m.ctc equals 1
  definition m.odc equals 1
  definition m.agi equals $210,000
  definition m.tax equals $30,000
  assertion m.s.total_potential_dependent_credits = $2,500
  assertion m.s.dependent_credit_phaseout = $500
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $2,000
  assertion m.s.total_odc = $0
  assertion m.s.total_ctc = $2,000
  assertion m.s.is_receiving_ctc
  assertion not m.s.is_receiving_odc
```

### ODC only: no ACTC

The ACTC is for qualifying children only (IRC 24(h)(5)(A) "without regard to
paragraph (4)"; instructions p 2: "you cannot take the ACTC if you are only
claiming the ODC").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812OdcOnlyNoActc:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812OdcOnlyNoActc:
  definition m.ctc equals 0
  definition m.odc equals 1
  definition m.tax equals $200
  assertion m.s.total_potential_odc = $500
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $200
  assertion m.s.total_odc = $200
  assertion m.s.remaining_ctc_and_odc = $300
  assertion m.s.total_potential_actc = $0
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $0
```

## Part II: the additional child tax credit

### Earned income $2,500: no ACTC; $10,000: $7,500 x 15% = $1,125

Two CTC children, no tax: line 16a = $4,000, line 16b = $3,400, line 17 =
$3,400. Line 19 is blank (not more than $2,500) or $7,500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812ActcEarnedIncome:
  e2500 scope Mk8812
  e10000 scope Mk8812

scope Test8812ActcEarnedIncome:
  definition e2500.agi equals $2,500
  definition e2500.earned equals $2,500
  definition e2500.tax equals $0
  definition e10000.agi equals $10,000
  definition e10000.earned equals $10,000
  definition e10000.tax equals $0
  assertion e2500.s.remaining_potential_actc = $3,400
  assertion e2500.s.earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold = $0
  assertion not e2500.s.earned_income_exceeds_actc_refundability_threshold
  assertion e2500.s.regular_maximum_actc = $0
  assertion e2500.s.additional_ctc = $0
  assertion e10000.s.earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold = $7,500
  assertion e10000.s.regular_maximum_actc = $1,125
  assertion e10000.s.additional_ctc = $1,125
  # Known-bad: 15% of all earned income ($1,500) is not the ACTC
  assertion e10000.s.additional_ctc != $1,500
```

### Combat pay counts as earned income (IRC 24(d)(1) last sentence, section 112)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812CombatPay:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812CombatPay:
  definition m.agi equals $10,000
  definition m.earned equals $10,000
  definition m.combat_pay equals $4,000
  definition m.tax equals $0
  assertion m.s.earned_income_with_all_combat_pay = $14,000
  assertion m.s.regular_maximum_actc = $1,725
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $1,725
```

### Three or more children: social security taxes less the EIC

Earned income $3,000 (line 20 = $75). Social security and Medicare taxes
withheld $230, no EIC (for example a filer whose investment income passes
$11,600). With three CTC children line 25 = $230 and line 26 = $230; with two
children Part II-B does not apply and line 27 is $75. With EIC $200 line 25
is $30 and line 26 is line 20, $75.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812ThreeKidsAlternative:
  three scope Mk8812
  two scope Mk8812
  three_with_eic scope Mk8812

scope Test8812ThreeKidsAlternative:
  definition three.ctc equals 3
  definition three.agi equals $20,000
  definition three.earned equals $3,000
  definition three.ss_taxes equals $230
  definition three.tax equals $0
  definition two.agi equals $20,000
  definition two.earned equals $3,000
  definition two.ss_taxes equals $230
  definition two.tax equals $0
  definition three_with_eic.ctc equals 3
  definition three_with_eic.agi equals $20,000
  definition three_with_eic.earned equals $3,000
  definition three_with_eic.ss_taxes equals $230
  definition three_with_eic.eic equals $200
  definition three_with_eic.tax equals $0
  assertion three.s.regular_maximum_actc = $75
  assertion three.s.three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents
  assertion three.s.social_security_over_eitc = $230
  assertion three.s.maximum_actc = $230
  assertion three.s.additional_ctc = $230
  assertion not two.s.three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents
  assertion two.s.maximum_actc = $75
  assertion two.s.additional_ctc = $75
  # Known-bad: the alternative does not apply to two children
  assertion two.s.additional_ctc != $230
  assertion three_with_eic.s.social_security_over_eitc = $30
  assertion three_with_eic.s.additional_ctc = $75
```

### Line 17 caps the ACTC at $1,700 per child

One CTC child, no tax, earned income $40,000: line 20 = $5,625, line 16b =
$1,700. Line 27 = $1,700, not $2,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812ActcCap:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812ActcCap:
  definition m.ctc equals 1
  definition m.agi equals $40,000
  definition m.earned equals $40,000
  definition m.tax equals $0
  assertion m.s.remaining_ctc_and_odc = $2,000
  assertion m.s.total_potential_actc = $1,700
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $1,700
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc != $2,000
```

## Improper claims (IRC 24(g))

### Inside a 2-year ban: no CTC, ODC or ACTC

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812ImproperClaimsBan:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812ImproperClaimsBan:
  definition m.odc equals 1
  definition m.tax equals $0
  definition m.received_improper_claims equals true
  definition m.notice equals E.ImproperClaimsNotice.TwoYears
  assertion m.s.ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims
  assertion m.s.total_potential_ctc = $0
  assertion m.s.total_potential_odc = $0
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $0
  assertion m.s.additional_ctc = $0
  assertion not m.s.ctc8862_required
```

### The ban expired: the credit is allowed and Form 8862 is required

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Test8812ImproperClaimsExpired:
  m scope Mk8812

scope Test8812ImproperClaimsExpired:
  definition m.received_improper_claims equals true
  definition m.notice equals E.ImproperClaimsNotice.TwoYears
  definition m.notice_expired equals true
  assertion not m.s.ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims
  assertion m.s.total_ctc_and_odc = $4,000
  assertion m.s.ctc8862_required
```
